WEBVTT

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:18.490
<b>3:38 PM, Itabashi Ward</b>

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:26.750
<b>3:38 PM, Komae City</b>

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:30.210
Wait, is he causing the traffic jam?

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:36.340
<b>3:38 PM, Chiyoda Ward</b>

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:39.300
<b>3:38 PM, Shinagawa Ward</b>

00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:49.930
The Willwear that broke the Itabashi 
Ward's convenience store windows

00:00:49.930 --> 00:00:52.920
is on the move near 
Nishi-Takashimadaira Station.

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:54.490
And Chiyoda and Shinagawa Wards?

00:00:54.730 --> 00:00:55.990
Wait.

00:00:55.990 --> 00:00:58.450
I just got word from Funabashi and Matsudo.

00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:00.580
Um, we're getting requests for help from

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:02.870
Higashiyamato and Warabi, too.

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:05.160
Why is all this happening at once?

00:01:05.430 --> 00:01:07.620
They're appearing in different spots 
and doing different things.

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:08.730
Where's the video?

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:10.590
We don't have video from anywhere yet?

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:13.340
Everyone's in a panic.

00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:15.700
Is this crime being done by a team?

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:16.300
Boss?

00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:18.410
Which track should the command vehicle use?

00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:19.490
Um...

00:01:19.490 --> 00:01:22.810
We'll start by going to the special 
standby platform in Kichijouji.

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:25.030
We'll all head out at once.

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:26.020
But...

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:29.420
We don't have enough people, do we?

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.090
<i>In the future,</i>

00:01:35.090 --> 00:01:38.510
<i>when something happens beyond 
the normal police's capacity,</i>

00:01:38.510 --> 00:01:41.370
<i>they turn to the power of the ACTIVE project.</i>

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:47.710
<i>This is the story of Japan's ACTIVE, 
the Third Mobile Assault Unit.</i>

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:05.030
<b>File 5: Who Benefits?</b>

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:09.040
I never expected to see multiple 
Willwear crimes at once.

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:09.870
<b>Requesting</b>

00:03:09.350 --> 00:03:10.520
What shall we do?

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:10.750
<b>Connection Approved</b>

00:03:10.520 --> 00:03:11.870
Take them in the order they came in?

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:12.990
Yes.

00:03:12.990 --> 00:03:16.880
We'll just have to let the local police 
handle it until we arrive.

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:19.920
Let's just have everyone prepare 
to launch, starting with Oscar I.

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:21.090
Understood.

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:23.890
Kenzou-san, start heading back.

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:25.200
Unit 8 is coming.

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:27.850
Kogure-kun, get out of there in three minutes.

00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:28.470
And...

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:35.660
Where's the criminal?

00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:37.050
You're late!

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:39.120
What are you doing?

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:40.840
He already ran!

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:42.320
H-He ran?

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:44.840
Oscar II, is your criminal still there?

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:47.660
Wait, you too, Oscar V?

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:48.350
Yeah.

00:03:48.350 --> 00:03:49.860
It's the same with everyone.

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:51.620
We all missed them.

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:52.870
Damn!

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:56.430
It's like they knew when we'd get here!

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:05.180
That's from the incident before, right?

00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:07.480
What did they want to accomplish?

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:10.240
Who cares? Let's go.

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:12.890
Chiiko's concert is going to start!

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:24.740
What is this?

00:04:25.510 --> 00:04:27.950
Are live clubs usually like this?

00:04:29.340 --> 00:04:31.690
Chiiko's might be a little special.

00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:53.280
<i>The children die with their guts ripped out.</i>

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:59.790
<i>Once again, the world is covered 
in blood, beneath the blue sky.</i>

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:01.110
Is that Chiiko?

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:04.320
Yeah, her name's Mibu Chiiko, 
so her stage name is Mivv.

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:08.320
<i>But you useless pigs just do</i>

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:14.900
<i>what those bastards in 
the system tell you to.</i>

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:11.940
Crazy, isn't it?

00:05:11.940 --> 00:05:14.000
Nothing like when she was in school!

00:05:15.550 --> 00:05:17.310
<i>Kiss my ass.</i>

00:05:17.310 --> 00:05:22.650
<i>The world is full of shit,</i>

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:29.580
<i>but at least I can wrap myself 
in your intestines!</i>

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:38.780
<i>Just slice your belly open, yank out 
your organs, and throw them away.</i>

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:35.410
Slice it open!

00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:38.780
Throw them away!

00:05:38.780 --> 00:05:45.040
<i>You can be the real you.</i>

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:48.730
Hinata?

00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:50.960
Hinata?!

00:05:53.910 --> 00:05:57.660
<i>There were more simultaneous Willwear crimes</i>

00:05:53.910 --> 00:06:12.390
<b>Simultaneous 
Willwear Crimes
Citizens fed up with useless police</b>

00:05:56.500 --> 00:06:12.390
<b>Your Morning Show</b>

00:05:57.660 --> 00:05:59.570
<i>just a while ago, I heard.</i>

00:05:59.570 --> 00:06:02.920
<i>Yes, a Willwear carrying a fire extinguisher</i>

00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:04.960
<i>sprayed foam everywhere, for instance.</i>

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:07.250
<i>Well, I hate to say it,</i>

00:06:07.250 --> 00:06:09.510
<i>but these are all small-scale crimes.</i>

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:12.390
<i>In one Machida case, they rang 
a doorbell and ran away.</i>

00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:17.080
<i>The problem is how useless Unit 8 is, though.</i>

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:20.500
<i>They've always arrived too late, 
and haven't caught a single one.</i>

00:06:20.810 --> 00:06:21.900
Damn them!

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:23.890
They don't have a clue.

00:06:23.890 --> 00:06:28.040
But it's not as if they're 
giving false information.

00:06:28.040 --> 00:06:29.630
What are they after?

00:06:29.630 --> 00:06:31.620
Maybe society-wide unrest.

00:06:31.980 --> 00:06:36.000
It's like they just want to shake up the system.

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:41.400
If we could capture even one, 
we might get somewhere.

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:44.460
If only we could get there 
first and set an ambush...

00:06:44.680 --> 00:06:45.600
That's it!

00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:53.250
Huh? I...

00:06:55.180 --> 00:06:57.350
I'm so sorry. Are you okay?

00:06:58.790 --> 00:07:00.070
Chiiko?

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:01.640
That's...

00:07:01.640 --> 00:07:03.620
Was that a little too much?

00:07:03.620 --> 00:07:06.170
Well, I mean, it...

00:07:06.170 --> 00:07:07.870
It was great!

00:07:07.870 --> 00:07:09.070
Just like Hell.

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:11.620
Well, this is normal.

00:07:11.920 --> 00:07:14.780
Many people do extreme performance art.

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:16.910
<b>You can join the Sabbath, too!</b>

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:16.490
I'm really happy, though!

00:07:16.490 --> 00:07:20.440
Hardly any of my old classmates 
come to my performances!

00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:22.790
<b>You can join the Sabbath, too! 
Contact Info for Demons 
Ask the Demons How to Get There 
From Kichijouji Station North Exit: 4 minutes, 27 seconds walk 
Location: Concert Hall Demon Soul</b>

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:22.270
But you're working so hard!

00:07:22.270 --> 00:07:24.470
Weren't you on the news, too?

00:07:22.790 --> 00:07:28.130
<b>Contact Info for Demons 
Ask the Demons How to Get There 
From Kichijouji Station North Exit: 4 min. 27 sec. walk 
Location: Live Club Demon Soul</b>

00:07:24.790 --> 00:07:27.350
As, like, the anti-establishment
underground idol!

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:29.160
Yes?

00:07:31.950 --> 00:07:34.350
Are you done? Other people are waiting.

00:07:34.900 --> 00:07:37.060
Pardon us. We'll be going.

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:39.640
Sorry I can't talk more!

00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:41.010
Don't worry.

00:07:41.980 --> 00:07:43.000
I see...

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:45.440
So this is what you wanted to do.

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:49.490
This has my concert schedule.

00:07:49.490 --> 00:07:50.440
Come see me again?

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:55.300
Um, it looks like the ambush isn't going to work.

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:55.620
<b>Unit 8</b>

00:07:55.850 --> 00:07:59.080
The Tokyo government isn't interested 
in anything without precedent.

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:00.270
No way!

00:08:00.270 --> 00:08:02.180
Man, that's bureaucrats for you.

00:08:02.180 --> 00:08:04.920
Fine, I guess we'll talk to Inagi-kun.

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:07.830
It's pretty handy to have 
the governor on speed dial.

00:08:07.830 --> 00:08:12.130
U-Um, he's the one against it, supposedly.

00:08:12.410 --> 00:08:14.410
Inagi-san is? Why?

00:08:14.410 --> 00:08:16.150
I wasn't told why.

00:08:19.140 --> 00:08:21.390
I remember now. That guy...

00:08:21.390 --> 00:08:22.960
Wasn't he Mivv's manager?

00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:24.030
Do you know him?

00:08:24.030 --> 00:08:26.260
His name's Kondou-san, I think.

00:08:26.260 --> 00:08:27.500
He's two years older.

00:08:27.800 --> 00:08:31.110
He was famous for extreme political actions.

00:08:31.680 --> 00:08:33.260
He was a student at our school?

00:08:33.260 --> 00:08:34.150
Yeah.

00:08:39.850 --> 00:08:41.510
Trying to reach Inagi-san?

00:08:41.510 --> 00:08:42.820
He's not picking up.

00:08:42.820 --> 00:08:44.700
Well, he's the governor.

00:08:44.700 --> 00:08:45.790
He must be busy.

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:47.010
I'm sure.

00:08:47.310 --> 00:08:50.150
But I wonder if there's some reason.

00:08:50.150 --> 00:08:53.880
He probably isn't opposed to the 
idea for personal reasons.

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:55.630
We don't know that.

00:08:56.200 --> 00:08:59.390
Haven't you heard people say that the 
Tokyo government does too much,

00:08:59.390 --> 00:09:02.610
and the opposing factions are 
starting to come together?

00:09:02.610 --> 00:09:05.100
So he's opposed out of self-preservation?

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:07.400
No way. Not Inagi-san.

00:09:07.790 --> 00:09:10.350
You really trust Inagi-kun, huh?

00:09:10.350 --> 00:09:14.110
Honestly, I owe him a lot.

00:09:14.110 --> 00:09:18.510
Why must I take out the trash for people 
who are too lazy to do it themselves?

00:09:18.510 --> 00:09:21.750
You really like Inagi-kun.

00:09:22.740 --> 00:09:24.360
Did something happen a long time ago?

00:09:24.360 --> 00:09:25.360
Well...

00:09:26.710 --> 00:09:30.040
I got involved in something really stupid once.

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:34.420
What is this, Kuroki?

00:09:34.420 --> 00:09:37.250
I thought you were joining our gang.

00:09:37.250 --> 00:09:40.010
So what are you doing with them?

00:09:40.310 --> 00:09:42.720
You said you were going to hurt them.

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:47.330
They snitched to the cops on us.

00:09:47.330 --> 00:09:49.810
Because you were causing a ruckus near them.

00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:53.780
They're orphans! They don't 
have the right to complain.

00:09:53.780 --> 00:09:56.770
Our tax money feeds them!

00:10:00.280 --> 00:10:02.530
This isn't cool.

00:10:04.820 --> 00:10:05.970
You guys...

00:10:06.760 --> 00:10:08.580
You don't even pay taxes, do you?

00:10:08.860 --> 00:10:10.950
What are you trying to say?

00:10:10.950 --> 00:10:12.340
That your gang is shit,

00:10:12.340 --> 00:10:14.630
and I'm glad I didn't join it!

00:10:16.190 --> 00:10:17.340
You bastard!

00:10:18.870 --> 00:10:19.790
Jackass!

00:10:21.230 --> 00:10:22.180
Take this!

00:10:28.780 --> 00:10:30.150
Don't move, Kuroki!

00:10:32.010 --> 00:10:34.110
Think you can get away with that?

00:10:34.380 --> 00:10:34.940
Get him!

00:10:36.100 --> 00:10:37.650
You're dead!

00:10:46.510 --> 00:10:48.890
Show us how cool you can be.

00:10:48.890 --> 00:10:51.380
I wonder how much you can take.

00:11:03.460 --> 00:11:05.350
What's with those eyes?

00:11:05.350 --> 00:11:07.060
Don't screw with me!

00:11:11.620 --> 00:11:15.150
I wasn't a good kid back then.

00:11:15.690 --> 00:11:18.650
Even so, I couldn't stand bullying.

00:11:19.290 --> 00:11:21.660
But I didn't really think things through.

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:25.910
Huh?

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:27.310
Who the hell are you?

00:11:29.380 --> 00:11:31.210
And then he came.

00:11:37.750 --> 00:11:39.370
Who are you?

00:11:43.910 --> 00:11:45.830
He was teaching a lesson

00:11:45.830 --> 00:11:48.430
to people who dearly needed one.

00:11:49.390 --> 00:11:51.060
But he was naturally so brutal.

00:11:51.800 --> 00:11:53.500
To be honest, I was scared.

00:11:57.810 --> 00:11:58.310
Um—

00:11:58.310 --> 00:11:59.210
You...

00:11:59.620 --> 00:12:01.320
Which are you?

00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:08.950
You're famous around here, aren't you?

00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:12.120
Don't worry. It's not broken.

00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:13.420
It doesn't matter!

00:12:13.420 --> 00:12:15.090
It hurts!

00:12:15.390 --> 00:12:16.920
I'll take you to the hospital now.

00:12:17.380 --> 00:12:18.630
So answer me.

00:12:18.930 --> 00:12:22.130
Which path will you take?

00:12:23.600 --> 00:12:26.960
After that, whenever something 
happened, he'd beat me up.

00:12:26.960 --> 00:12:29.010
But he also looked out for me.

00:12:29.420 --> 00:12:32.170
He was always telling me to 
study or learn martial arts.

00:12:32.170 --> 00:12:33.910
The next thing I knew, I was a policeman.

00:12:33.910 --> 00:12:34.980
Oh?

00:12:35.260 --> 00:12:38.430
The day I got my commission, he gave me this.

00:12:35.690 --> 00:12:42.950
<b>Knight</b>

00:12:38.830 --> 00:12:40.820
He said he special-ordered it.

00:12:41.160 --> 00:12:42.950
He's kinda weird, huh?

00:12:42.950 --> 00:12:44.240
That actually happened?

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:45.180
Oh?

00:12:45.180 --> 00:12:46.210
H-Huh?

00:12:46.500 --> 00:12:48.090
But I don't know...

00:12:48.410 --> 00:12:51.620
Hearing that makes it harder 
for me to contact him.

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:52.940
It's not good for

00:12:52.940 --> 00:12:56.350
an officer to contact the governor 
whenever she needs something.

00:12:57.700 --> 00:12:59.590
Of course! We have...

00:12:59.990 --> 00:13:02.200
a civilian who doesn't need permission.

00:13:02.200 --> 00:13:02.830
Huh?

00:13:02.830 --> 00:13:04.050
Ready to work?

00:13:10.680 --> 00:13:15.020
Yo! I'm comin' at ya, shitbags!

00:13:15.030 --> 00:13:18.640
We're Senars, Inc., your one-stop source 
for trash pickup, sorting, cleaning,

00:13:18.640 --> 00:13:19.610
and banging your mom!

00:13:19.610 --> 00:13:20.730
Wow!

00:13:20.730 --> 00:13:23.860
We'll clean your filthy house 
or your filthy company!

00:13:23.860 --> 00:13:25.190
Whenever, wherever!

00:13:25.190 --> 00:13:27.070
Excuse me, trash lady!

00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:29.280
Oh, good...

00:13:29.620 --> 00:13:32.070
I couldn't get it ready by pickup time.

00:13:33.160 --> 00:13:34.700
Noncombustible, yes?

00:13:35.010 --> 00:13:36.120
Thank you.

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:41.750
Boss, are we really getting paid for this?

00:13:42.010 --> 00:13:45.510
Don't worry. Just focus on driving safely.

00:13:46.170 --> 00:13:49.510
There's no issue with a civilian 
agent using a Willwear,

00:13:49.860 --> 00:13:52.970
and criminals won't be looking out for one.

00:13:52.970 --> 00:13:55.930
The problem is that there's 
no one to relieve them.

00:13:55.930 --> 00:13:59.930
I hope we can find a pattern in the 
dates and times of the incidents.

00:13:59.930 --> 00:14:02.650
I couldn't find any particular pattern

00:14:02.650 --> 00:14:04.860
in the dates the criminals appeared.

00:14:07.800 --> 00:14:09.450
Kogure-kun, take Asao Ward.

00:14:09.110 --> 00:14:12.580
<b>Social Problems
Research Circle</b>

00:14:09.450 --> 00:14:10.850
Next is...

00:14:10.850 --> 00:14:12.580
Kenzou-san can take Fussa.

00:14:12.580 --> 00:14:14.540
Nocchi, Minamibousou.

00:14:14.540 --> 00:14:17.040
Kakiya, you take Izumi.

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:19.440
Okay. Now, listen up.

00:14:19.440 --> 00:14:23.080
We'll calculate the time it 
takes for Unit 8 to arrive.

00:14:23.080 --> 00:14:25.590
Make sure to withdraw when told to.

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:26.900
We know that.

00:14:27.230 --> 00:14:30.400
But Willwears are harder 
to use than I expected.

00:14:30.400 --> 00:14:33.600
Yeah, my legs swell up and get stiff.

00:14:33.600 --> 00:14:35.710
You're being properly compensated.

00:14:35.710 --> 00:14:36.830
Right, right.

00:14:36.830 --> 00:14:40.750
But this time, let Mivv-chan 
and me get a little more.

00:14:40.750 --> 00:14:43.130
Kenzou-san, you're too aggressive.

00:14:43.130 --> 00:14:46.570
Drawing a clear line between idol 
and fan is much more fun.

00:14:46.570 --> 00:14:48.060
Shut up!

00:14:49.740 --> 00:14:52.440
Everyone, thanks for coming again today!

00:14:54.040 --> 00:14:56.300
Be grateful to all of them.

00:14:56.300 --> 00:14:59.030
They're doing it for you.

00:14:59.030 --> 00:15:00.910
Kondou-san, a moment?

00:15:02.830 --> 00:15:05.360
Next time, can I sing this?

00:15:05.360 --> 00:15:06.730
I wrote some lyrics.

00:15:06.730 --> 00:15:07.590
Too normal.

00:15:08.190 --> 00:15:10.300
I'm writing some good ones now.

00:15:10.640 --> 00:15:12.330
Normal isn't good enough?

00:15:12.330 --> 00:15:14.010
I want to sing something honest.

00:15:14.340 --> 00:15:17.830
You've tried a cute one, a bullied one, 
a big eater, a military otaku...

00:15:17.830 --> 00:15:20.730
And all those characters failed.

00:15:20.730 --> 00:15:23.200
You need songs that make you stand out.

00:15:23.200 --> 00:15:24.970
But what are you doing now?

00:15:24.970 --> 00:15:27.440
Don't use my fans for weird stuff.

00:15:27.440 --> 00:15:28.510
Weird stuff?

00:15:28.510 --> 00:15:29.770
Don't be stupid!

00:15:29.770 --> 00:15:32.520
This is our chance to change the 
corrupt city government!

00:15:32.520 --> 00:15:34.760
We'll ruin Tokyo's law and order...

00:15:34.760 --> 00:15:39.040
But it feels like someone's using you.

00:15:39.390 --> 00:15:42.130
Where did you get those 
Willwears everyone's using?

00:15:42.130 --> 00:15:43.440
And if you get caught—

00:15:44.500 --> 00:15:46.470
They're misdemeanors.

00:15:46.470 --> 00:15:47.830
They'll get off easy.

00:15:48.130 --> 00:15:51.800
Listen, it's going well because 
I'm running things, right?

00:15:51.800 --> 00:15:54.240
So keep your mouth shut.

00:16:01.370 --> 00:16:03.680
No sign of them tonight, either.

00:16:03.680 --> 00:16:07.540
Oscar I's been out for 68 hours.

00:16:07.840 --> 00:16:09.490
Sorry, the mission's canceled.

00:16:09.490 --> 00:16:11.490
Tell Oscar I to come back.

00:16:13.700 --> 00:16:15.660
A-Are you all right?

00:16:15.660 --> 00:16:18.160
Of course he's not, you scumwad d**k!

00:16:18.160 --> 00:16:19.200
Scum—

00:16:23.830 --> 00:16:25.480
Jeez...

00:16:28.050 --> 00:16:30.510
<b>You can join the Sabbath, too!</b>

00:16:28.840 --> 00:16:30.400
A massage?

00:16:30.700 --> 00:16:31.970
No, that's not right.

00:16:32.760 --> 00:16:34.010
You're back?

00:16:34.310 --> 00:16:35.590
What's this?

00:16:36.060 --> 00:16:38.840
Oh, remember? I told you about it.

00:16:38.840 --> 00:16:41.350
It's a schedule for a friend's 
concerts and events.

00:16:41.350 --> 00:16:44.410
It's amazing! If you saw...

00:16:44.740 --> 00:16:45.830
Something wrong?

00:16:46.120 --> 00:16:47.440
<i>These dates...</i>

00:16:54.240 --> 00:17:00.910
<i>But you useless pigs just do</i>

00:17:00.910 --> 00:17:07.290
<i>what those bastards in 
the system tell you to.</i>

00:17:08.180 --> 00:17:10.180
<i>Kiss my ass.</i>

00:17:12.140 --> 00:17:13.220
Morning!

00:17:13.220 --> 00:17:14.420
Oh, boss...

00:17:14.420 --> 00:17:16.770
Sena-kun's left for the mission again.

00:17:16.770 --> 00:17:19.040
Sorry, I asked him to.

00:17:19.510 --> 00:17:20.680
Why?

00:17:20.680 --> 00:17:23.070
Weren't we going to try a different way?

00:17:23.070 --> 00:17:26.400
That's yesterday's plan, but I found 
something that might work.

00:17:26.400 --> 00:17:28.170
You're always such a big help.

00:17:28.170 --> 00:17:29.730
I was surprised at first, though.

00:17:29.730 --> 00:17:30.570
Aw...

00:17:31.490 --> 00:17:36.220
We actually hold on to our trash and 
save it for when you come through.

00:17:36.220 --> 00:17:38.730
Micchii-san was saying the same thing!

00:17:38.730 --> 00:17:40.330
You know, from Baba-san's place.

00:17:41.170 --> 00:17:42.000
Baba?!

00:17:42.000 --> 00:17:44.280
Hey, boss, did you poop your pants?

00:17:44.280 --> 00:17:45.160
I knew it!

00:17:45.560 --> 00:17:47.850
Four places are requesting aid.

00:17:47.850 --> 00:17:50.490
Yoyogi is the closest to Oscar I.

00:17:50.490 --> 00:17:51.690
What are they doing?

00:17:51.690 --> 00:17:53.880
Apparently, spreading trash everywhere.

00:17:54.660 --> 00:17:55.590
Trash?!

00:17:58.340 --> 00:17:59.360
There!

00:18:02.680 --> 00:18:05.560
All the crimes are occurring several hours

00:18:05.560 --> 00:18:08.020
after Hinata's friend's concerts or events.

00:18:08.270 --> 00:18:10.190
And today was a morning concert.

00:18:10.700 --> 00:18:13.250
The guys at the events are the criminals?

00:18:13.250 --> 00:18:16.610
That means the mastermind might be 
involved with the concert, as well?

00:18:16.610 --> 00:18:19.200
Oscar I will reach the scene in one minute!

00:18:19.740 --> 00:18:21.690
Unit 8 will be there in five minutes.

00:18:21.690 --> 00:18:22.990
Time to go.

00:18:22.990 --> 00:18:23.980
Got it.

00:18:23.980 --> 00:18:25.500
I'll be off.

00:18:32.100 --> 00:18:33.840
H-How?

00:18:33.840 --> 00:18:35.840
Hey! Unit 8 is already here!

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:36.670
What?

00:18:36.670 --> 00:18:40.950
I'm with Senars, Inc., a civilian company 
cooperating with the police.

00:18:40.950 --> 00:18:44.180
Please pick up the trash 
you scattered everywhere.

00:18:44.180 --> 00:18:45.850
How dare you—

00:18:45.850 --> 00:18:46.560
You want trash?!

00:18:48.150 --> 00:18:48.730
Why...

00:18:50.690 --> 00:18:52.690
Why can't you understand

00:18:52.690 --> 00:18:54.620
how hard the locals worked

00:18:54.620 --> 00:18:57.150
to pick all this garbage up from the street?

00:18:57.150 --> 00:19:00.610
Why don't you try to understand, you lowlife?!

00:19:04.530 --> 00:19:08.460
Clean up after yourself, you lazy boor!

00:19:11.630 --> 00:19:12.930
I'm sick of

00:19:12.930 --> 00:19:15.840
lazy boors like you!

00:19:17.100 --> 00:19:18.920
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:19:18.920 --> 00:19:19.890
I'm sorry!

00:19:18.920 --> 00:19:21.470
Everywhere I go, I see people like you!

00:19:22.920 --> 00:19:24.720
Die!

00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:25.760
Boss!

00:19:26.680 --> 00:19:28.560
You trying to kill him, you d**khead?!

00:19:41.160 --> 00:19:44.370
We haven't located the mastermind,

00:19:41.160 --> 00:19:45.200
<b>Name: Unknown 

00:19:44.370 --> 00:19:45.760
a man named Kondou.

00:19:45.760 --> 00:19:48.510
There's a good chance he fled the country.

00:19:48.510 --> 00:19:50.120
Did we learn his goal?

00:19:50.460 --> 00:19:53.950
Why would he do something so crazy?

00:19:53.950 --> 00:19:56.130
His aim was to disrupt law and order,

00:19:56.130 --> 00:19:58.850
and damage the people's faith 
in the city government.

00:19:58.850 --> 00:20:00.090
Seriously?

00:20:00.090 --> 00:20:01.640
Looks like it.

00:20:01.640 --> 00:20:05.010
He's been doing political stuff 
like this since high school.

00:20:05.010 --> 00:20:07.810
And he doesn't like the Inagi administration.

00:20:07.810 --> 00:20:11.440
But where did he get all the Willwears?

00:20:11.770 --> 00:20:13.690
What about the one I caught?

00:20:13.690 --> 00:20:17.210
The man you almost killed was 
Umegatani Kenzou, age 46.

00:20:16.480 --> 00:20:21.320
<b>Name: Umegatani Kenzou 

00:20:17.210 --> 00:20:19.360
He was a CG animator, single.

00:20:19.650 --> 00:20:23.910
They made him think he could get closer 
to the underground idol Mivv

00:20:23.910 --> 00:20:26.030
and convinced him to participate in the crimes.

00:20:26.280 --> 00:20:28.640
Just for something like that?

00:20:28.640 --> 00:20:31.500
I guess once he started, he couldn't stop.

00:20:31.770 --> 00:20:34.470
Everyone has their own set of values.

00:20:35.790 --> 00:20:38.050
<b>Inagi Koutaro 

00:20:36.810 --> 00:20:38.050
Inagi-kun?

00:20:38.050 --> 00:20:40.760
Sorry I couldn't take your call.

00:20:41.170 --> 00:20:43.280
I was busy dealing with the Diet.

00:20:43.280 --> 00:20:47.470
I didn't have any way to judge 
whether your idea was good.

00:20:47.760 --> 00:20:49.920
No, I'm sorry.

00:20:49.920 --> 00:20:51.560
I called you again and again.

00:20:51.560 --> 00:20:53.500
I think it was really arrogant.

00:20:53.500 --> 00:20:54.560
Not at all.

00:20:54.790 --> 00:20:57.070
But you made the right call.

00:20:57.070 --> 00:20:57.990
It really helped.

00:20:57.990 --> 00:20:58.550
Huh?

00:20:59.020 --> 00:21:02.080
Sena-kun, the civilian cooperator, 
solved the case.

00:21:02.630 --> 00:21:05.970
It's a big accomplishment for us 
to boast about. Thanks. Bye.

00:21:08.060 --> 00:21:11.700
So, it all worked out for Inagi-san, huh?

00:21:11.700 --> 00:21:12.940
I guess so.

00:21:12.940 --> 00:21:15.200
Now all that's left is the person behind it.

00:21:15.500 --> 00:21:17.640
Think it's Hachijou?

00:21:17.640 --> 00:21:18.420
Who knows?

00:21:18.420 --> 00:21:19.550
Either way,

00:21:19.810 --> 00:21:23.070
this Kondou guy was just being used.

00:21:23.070 --> 00:21:25.800
Mivv was the one who was really being used.

00:21:26.470 --> 00:21:28.260
She's Hinata's friend.

00:21:28.260 --> 00:21:30.560
They acted like she was special and used her...

00:21:30.940 --> 00:21:33.180
Acted like she was special, huh?

00:21:35.020 --> 00:21:37.310
I hope she recovers...

00:21:35.480 --> 00:21:37.020
<b>Jirou             Shinjirou</b>

00:21:37.020 --> 00:21:39.650
<b>Jirou             Shinjirou 

00:21:37.810 --> 00:21:38.600
Yeah.

00:21:48.130 --> 00:21:49.530
Chiiko?

00:21:49.530 --> 00:21:52.430
I'm glad you're doing better, Mivv-chan!

00:21:52.430 --> 00:21:55.750
You, too! I'm glad you were released!

00:21:55.750 --> 00:21:58.500
A few of us are still in jail.

00:21:58.500 --> 00:22:01.960
Mivv-chan, we'll support you 
with your next character!

00:22:02.460 --> 00:22:03.510
<i>Kondou-san...</i>

00:22:04.250 --> 00:22:08.010
<i>Maybe I was used for your dream.</i>

00:22:08.960 --> 00:22:11.140
<i>But I will use</i>

00:22:11.380 --> 00:22:13.390
<i>the opportunity you gave me.</i>

00:22:15.900 --> 00:22:18.820
<i>Thank you, Terrorist-san!</i>

00:23:50.030 --> 00:23:51.700
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:51.590 --> 00:23:52.890
Ohakonyapachininko.

00:23:52.360 --> 00:24:04.910
File 6: Rudra Strikes Back

00:23:52.890 --> 00:23:55.240
Boss, what are you saying? D**k in p**sy?

00:23:55.240 --> 00:23:57.830
No! Don't say stuff that'll get us in trouble!

00:23:57.830 --> 00:24:00.310
Forget that! Next time, our company's in trouble!

00:24:00.310 --> 00:24:01.540
Ram your d**k in!

00:24:01.540 --> 00:24:03.330
This preview is terrible!
